// Ateula, Vellaunos's daughter, seventeen, clerk to the quartermaster.
// She may stay. If she does, she gives the hostage roll. She can also
// write a release order, given a seal that isn't hers.
=== start
[flag met_ateula] -> again
~ set met_ateula
A young woman at the end of Orbius's table is copying a roll from one tablet to another, very fast, without looking up. A plain Roman dress, ink on her fingers, a stylus behind her ear.

"You're from Brigodunon." She still doesn't look up. "You stand like my father." Then she does look up, and she has his eyes, the grain-weighing look. "I'm Ateula. You know that. You're here for Eponina."

"And for you."

"Yes," she says. "I thought you'd say that."
-> hub

=== again
[flag ateula_out] -> END
[flag ateula_stays] "Still here?" She doesn't stop writing. "So am I."
[!flag ateula_stays] "Cadurci." She doesn't stop writing.
